==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Dr. Mekako''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Mission Control Mekako''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Mekako has drastically changing gameplay styles throughout each of her forms, each one serving an anti-Alien role. She doesn't have any stat changes between forms, so if you're using her for generalist purposes it's best to use her first form for the ability to survive.

Speaking of those generalist purposes, she is replaceable, but 4.7k DPS and 445 range is enough to get things done. You don't need to use her as a generalist, but you shouldn't avoid doing so either. She's pretty decent!

==='''Normal Form'''===
Mekako in her normal gear functions as a tanker. Unlike the other forms, this one targets an additional trait, that being Dark. While tanking Aliens can be hard when you don't have immunities, and tanking Darks is hard when you're able to be crushed easily, she definitely works. Her Survive ability is especially good in this form, allowing her to continue using her DPS. Overall, a decent anti-Alien/anti-Dark.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Mekako changes her usage from a tanker to a crowd-controller. While knocking back Aliens sounds troublesome, Mekako also has a chance to weaken them. That, and given her good enough range and lack of slow ability, makes her less likely to suffer the problems faced by [[Mizli (Uber Rare Cat)|Marinmizu]]. That ability still doesn't make her viable against Aliens, so all in all, this is the weakest of Mekako's forms.

==='''True Form'''===
Mekako, now with a better crowd-controlling ability, also gets massive damage to aliens as well. Her great range and better abilities make her a beast against Aliens. This True Form is certainly one worth getting, mainly because of the better compatibility with Aliens. Arguably, the compatibility is spectacular instead of just "better", and Mekako can easily become a go-to anti-Alien.

==='''Talents'''===
While giving Mekako Knockback again stiffens a whole lot of usage, giving her weaken and survive back sure doesn't. In fact, now she has the chance to become the ultimate crowd-controlling anti-Alien. Slow, combined with massive damage, combined with potential weaken gives her such good usage against Aliens that it's absurd. She has enough distance to avoid certain [[:Category:Enemies with Warp ability|enemies with Warp]], so her viability against [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]] is also very good.

Because her generalist usage was decent to begin with, the Attack and HP Buffs won't go to waste, even if the NP may be better spent elsewhere. It's worth getting the True Form for what it offers, but the Talents make it even more worth it.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
Given how powerful her specialist performance is against Aliens, '''Target [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]''' is top priority. Mekako's matchups are generally favorable across the board: instantly thwarting hordes of melees like [[Angelic Gory]] and [[St. Dober]] dead in their tracks, striking ranged attackers like [[Angelic Sleipnir]] and [[Winged Pigge]] from a safe distance, and just generally crowd-controlling those she doesn't immediately eviscerate with her damage. Pairing this up with her other Talents, such as Weaken and/or Knockback, makes her a superlative nuker despite the competition.

'''[[Dodge Attack]]''' is a bit more dubious, especially for such a high NP cost. You already don't want her taking any hits at all, but this Ultra Talent serves as extra assurance against piercers of her traits (e.g., [[Xenobeast Bunaglios]], [[Crustaceous Scissorex]], St. Dober, [[Tarsiriel]], etc.), and should enemies begin encroaching within her space. At 50% it's actually quite high, especially considering her abnormally high base HP at Lv.60, so it can potentially make her completely immortal in the right circumstances. If you have the spare NP, there's no reason not to invest.

