==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Mekako Saionji was a part of three other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Overhaul (Removed Combo)|Overhaul]], [[Just Us League (Removed Combo)|Just Us League]] and [[Revengers (Removed Combo)|Revengers]].
*Prior to [[Version 14.3 Update|Version 14.3]], Mission Control Mekako was one of the few [[:Category:Cats with Ultra Talents|Cats with Ultra Talents]] to lack a second [[Talent Orbs|Talent Orb]] slot.
*She is the one of the few [[Justice Strikes Back! Dark Heroes (Gacha Event)|Dark Heroes]] not to contain a reference to darkness in their Evolved Form's name.
*Her Normal Form is one of the only units to have their abilities separated by a period in their description.
*Both Mission Control Mekako and [[Akira (Uber Rare Cat)|Inferno Akira]] regain their prior forms' abilities through [[Talents]].
*The name Mekako is a portmanteau of メカ ''meka'', meaning "mechanic", and 子 ''ko'', a suffix commonly used in female Japanese given names.
*In all three forms, the mech's overall shape is similar to the combined [[wikia:dragonball:Pilaf Machine|Pilaf Machines]] from ''Dragon Ball''.
*Mechanix Monthly may be a reference to the science and technology magazine ''[[wikipedia:Mechanix Illustrated|Mechanix Illustrated]]''.
*One of the possible endings for [[Gamatoto Expedition]] log messages is "in Mekako's workshop."

